<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">consider</ansi>

Size up an enemy before you fight it. Your company weighs itself, as it
stands now, against the enemy's whole group: a company fights together,
so there is no one-on-one guess. It is free and instant.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">consider [enemy]</ansi>
  Name a group (<ansi fg="command">consider ruffians</ansi>) or any one of its members
  (<ansi fg="command">consider ruffian</ansi>); a lone creature is a group of one.

  You consider a band of ruffians...
  Assessment: A fair fight for your company; the odds look clear.
    Counted: you, Tamsin Reed and Brother Oswin.
    Not judged: spells, healing and abilities, hidden foes, and anyone yet to come.
  Type scout ruffians to see how they stand.

The words run from an easy fight, a fair fight, and a hard fight to a grave
risk and hopeless, and never show numbers (<ansi fg="command">help assessment</ansi> explains
them and what is weighed). <ansi fg="command">scout [group]</ansi> gives the same assessment
under the group's formation.

You see what <ansi fg="command">look</ansi> sees: hidden foes are left out, and in the dark you
can't make them out. Other players aren't enemies to consider.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help assessment</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help scout</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
